The server's time is its request handler (NVTX `bench/request`). Kernel time counts concurrent kernels separately, so the total above exceeds the server's time by their overlap. A kernel gets its phase and section from the NVTX range around its launch call; {{ profile.unknown }} of {{ profile.count | num(0) }} kernels had no unambiguous launch range and are listed as Unknown. Other time gets the innermost phase and section range, on any thread, that covers it; outside every range, it is "{{ no_phase }}" and "{{ no_section }}".

Launch calls per request: {{ "%g" | format(profile.launches.kernel) }} kernel launches and {{ "%g" | format(profile.launches.graph) }} CUDA graph launches; the kernels inside a graph need no call of their own.

| Longest-running kernels | Family | ms per request | Launches per request |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |
{% for kernel in profile.kernels %}
| {{ kernel.name | code | cell }} | {{ kernel.family }} | {{ kernel.ms | num(3) }} | {{ "%g" | format(kernel.launches) }} |
{% endfor %}

Families come from kernel names only: GEMMs of different layers (QKV, MLP, LM head) look alike, so they share `linear`. The sunburst shows the families of each phase and section.

